# pnpm guidelines

Use pnpm for all package management and script execution. Do not use npm, yarn, bun, npx, or node for install, run, or tooling.

```bash
# ✅
pnpm install
pnpm add <pkg>
pnpm add -D <pkg>
pnpm remove <pkg>
pnpm run <script>
pnpm exec <cli>
pnpm dlx <cli>
pnpm test

# ❌
npm install / yarn install / bun install
npx ...
node ...
```

Prefer `pnpm dlx` over `npx` for one-off CLIs (including shadcn). Prefer `pnpm run` for package scripts.

## Electron Forge compatibility

This project uses Electron Forge, which requires specific pnpm settings:

- `nodeLinker: hoisted` in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` (and `node-linker=hoisted` in `.npmrc`)
- `blockExoticSubdeps: false` in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` (Forge pulls `@electron/node-gyp` from git)

Do not change these without verifying Forge still packages correctly.
